codebase-graph native CLI

USAGE:
  codebase-graph <command> [options]

COMMANDS:
  install                     Perform first-time graph setup and write .codebaseGraph/config.json
  reinstall                   Remove existing graph state and run install again
  uninstall                   Remove repo graph state, instructions, and MCP registrations
  agent-hooks                 Install, remove, verify, or run repository agent-loop hooks
  build                       Materialize a graph through the Rust native engine
  plan                        Preview files that would rebuild, delete, skip, or ignore
  watch                       Watch for file changes and refresh after a debounce window
  check-health                Check whether the native graph database is readable
  schema                      Return ontology schema, indexes, profiles, and helpers
  syntax                      Return a language syntax catalog
  query-helpers               Return named read-only graph query helpers
  codebase-architecture-queries  Return the architecture-discovery query catalog
  codebase-search             Search the code graph with compact context
  codebase-context            Return compact graph context
  graph-query                 Execute a restricted read-only graph query
  mcp                         Serve codebaseGraph MCP over stdio or HTTP

Run `codebase-graph <command> --help` for command options.
NATIVE_EXIT_STATUS=0
